---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import DocSection from '../components/DocSection.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';

const recognition = [
  'Specialist of the Quarter (x2) and Specialist of the Year',
  'Ricoh STAR Award',
  'Microsoft Azure Fundamentals, plus multiple enterprise product certifications',
];
---

<Layout title="About · Maxfield Allison" description="I'm Maxfield. I work with enterprise customers on Azure platforms, run a homelab, and write about what I'm figuring out." ogImage="/og/about.png?v=3">
  <article class="page-shell pt-16 pb-8">
    <div class="grid gap-4 md:gap-10 md:grid-cols-[var(--rail)_minmax(0,1fr)]">
    <p class="eyebrow md:pt-5">About Me</p>
    <div>
    <h1 class="font-serif text-[2.75rem] leading-tight mt-4 mb-8">Maxfield Allison</h1>
    <div class="measure space-y-5 text-[var(--color-ink-dim)] leading-relaxed">
      <p class="text-xl font-serif text-[var(--color-ink)]">I design enterprise infrastructure, argue for it, and then run it.</p>
      <p>I've spent ten years working with enterprise customers, starting in field support and becoming the global owner of an output-management platform on Azure. It serves thousands of devices across four regions. When it stops, people can't print, and in parts of that business printing isn't optional.</p>
      <p>I'm the person an issue comes to when the regional teams need help, and I approve production changes to the platform. That often means following a problem into a system another team owns. In one case, stopping our application services made DNS work again. Starting them brought the failures back. I worked through it with the firewall vendor and the customer's security team until we found the configuration faults and got them corrected.</p>
      <p>I've also been involved in the architecture decisions, from the move into Azure to regional redundancy. When we needed a test environment, I worked out the design and resource requirements across three organizations and made the business case that got it funded. The platform teams own the provisioning. <a href="/projects/test-environment">Getting it approved</a> took a lot more work than the design.</p>
      <p>Better documentation and self-service have been a big part of the job too. Platform support tickets fell 38% year over year, measured in the customer's ServiceNow. I'm now reworking the account's operational information so AI agents and Microsoft Power Automate flows have something useful to work from.</p>
    </div>
    </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <DocSection label="The Tools" spacing="tight">
    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold mb-4 mt-0">How I Use AI</h2>
    <div class="measure space-y-5 text-[var(--color-ink-dim)] leading-relaxed">
      <p>I use AI a lot, and I spend a lot of that time asking questions. What already exists? Why this approach? What would make it fail? Agents can investigate those questions and implement changes while I work through the choices with them. With dnsweaver, they write the code. I decide what the tool should do and whether it's ready for a release.</p>
      <p>That gives me room to explore things I might otherwise leave alone, or to have a proposed design challenged before committing to it. I still need to understand the system well enough to make the call. I've written more about <a href="https://probablyfine.dev/blog/how-i-use-ai?utm_source=maxfieldallison&utm_medium=site&utm_campaign=about" data-umami-event="outbound-probablyfine">how I use AI</a> and the parts of this process I'm still figuring out.</p>
    </div>
  </DocSection>

  <DocSection label="At Home" spacing="tight">
    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold mb-4 mt-0">Still Playing with Computers</h2>
    <div class="measure space-y-5 text-[var(--color-ink-dim)] leading-relaxed">
      <p>Games got me into computers long before I had a job working with them. I played DOS games beside my mom, learned to fix my own machines, and eventually hosted servers for friends. <a href="https://probablyfine.dev/blog/i-just-wanted-to-play-games?utm_source=maxfieldallison&utm_medium=site&utm_campaign=about" data-umami-event="outbound-probablyfine">I just wanted to play games</a> is the start of that story.</p>
      <p>The homelab came later, initially so I could watch movies. Now I'm hosting AI services and working on self-hosted replacements for the things I'd otherwise use Google for. There's Kubernetes and a Proxmox cluster with Ceph underneath, which is quite a lot of infrastructure for a hobby. I enjoy it. Some of what I learn turns out to be useful at work, but I'd be doing this regardless.</p>
    </div>
  </DocSection>

  <DocSection label="Experience" spacing="tight">
    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold mb-4 mt-0">Experience</h2>
    <p class="measure text-[var(--color-ink-dim)] leading-relaxed">My resume has <a href="/resume">the roles, projects, and technical detail</a>, including the path from field support to the work I do now.</p>
    <h3 class="font-serif text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3">Recognition</h3>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-[var(--color-ink-dim)] leading-relaxed">
      {recognition.map((r) => <li>{r}</li>)}
    </ul>
  </DocSection>

  <DocSection label="Say Hello" spacing="tight">
    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold mb-4 mt-0">Let’s Talk</h2>
    <p class="measure text-[var(--color-ink-dim)] leading-relaxed mb-4">If there's a project or a role you think I'd be a good fit for, I'd like to hear about it.</p>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-3 text-sm">
      <a href="mailto:maxfield.allison@gmail.com" data-umami-event="email-click" class="inline-flex items-center min-h-11 gap-1.5"><Icon name="email" size={14} /> Email</a>
      <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/maxfield-allison/" rel="me noopener" data-umami-event="outbound-linkedin" class="inline-flex items-center min-h-11 gap-1.5"><Icon name="linkedin" size={14} /> LinkedIn</a>
      <a href="https://bsky.app/profile/maxfieldallison.com" rel="me noopener" data-umami-event="outbound-bluesky" class="inline-flex items-center min-h-11 gap-1.5"><Icon name="bluesky" size={14} /> Bluesky</a>
    </div>
  </DocSection>
</Layout>
